  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `camcraft-motion`: new `sinker_side::side_burn_worn`. The plunge is the layered, wear-compensated plunge of `sinker_wear::burn_compensated`, with all of its refusals (rate, layer step, electrode length, deepest-tip bound). The lateral move and its return run at the last compensated tip. The tip is checked against the deepest-tip bound. With no wear and no layer step, the moves and notes are the same as `side_burn`.\n- `camcraft-app`: `SinkerSideBurnOp::refusal` no longer refuses a sound measured wear or layer step. The constants `SIDE_WEAR_REFUSAL` and `SIDE_LAYER_REFUSAL` are removed. A half-stated wear or a bad layer step is still refused by name (#546's refusals). `generate_sinker_side` calls `side_burn_worn` with `sinker_wear_op::side_wear` (the measured wear and the layer step only). `sinker_wear_op::judged` reads the side burn's moves as the worn electrode burns them, so the stock sim judges the real cavity.\n- `camcraft-ui`: the side burn page shows the Layer step, Measured wear and Measured over rows, with a wear status line (`side_wear_status`).\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/1340-side-burn-wear.md`. Only the measured wear applies to a side burn. The condition's `wear` rate is not applied, so a saved side burn posts byte for byte. Side wear is not compensated: a worn electrode is smaller, so the wall is left short, never cut past the allowance.\n\nThe MCP params door already carries `wear_lost`, `wear_over` and `layer` for a side burn: `SinkerSideDto` flattens the burn DTO (`project/sinker_dto.rs`). No new MCP tool is necessary.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `camcraft-motion` unit tests: `sinker_side_worn_off_is_the_plain_side_burn`, `sinker_side_worn_plunges_in_compensated_layers_and_moves_at_the_deepest_tip`, `sinker_side_worn_keeps_every_refusal_by_name`.\n- `crates/app/tests/sinker_side.rs`: `a_worn_side_burn_is_compensated_in_z_and_judged_clean` (replaces `a_side_burn_with_a_wear_rate_is_refused_by_name`). It checks the layer tips, the lateral move at the deepest tip, no move below that tip, a stock sim with no gouge, create/edit/paste/file doors, and that a condition's wear does not change a plain side burn.\n- The golden `sinker_side_burn.cl` is unchanged. `sinker_wear` suite is green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: green.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real EDM control. The fixtures are synthetic.\n- The UI rows were not opened in the GUI. No structural UI test was added for them.\n- Pixel snapshots (release lane).\n\nChangelog: A Sinker Side Burn takes a measured electrode wear and a layer step: the plunge is compensated in Z and the lateral move runs at the compensated tip (#1340)\n\nEffort: high\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #1340\n",
